Key Takeaways
A DevOps Engineer is responsible for automation, infrastructure, deployment, security, monitoring, and operational reliability.
The role spans the entire software delivery lifecycle.
Collaboration across multiple teams is a core part of the job.
Strong troubleshooting and automation skills are as important as knowing the tools.
